**HackUTD 2nd Place Winner (November 2026)**

House Rules is an autonomous roommate financial coordinator designed to bridge group communication with secure, private banking automation.

### Architecture & Implementation

- **Messaging Gateway**: Built in TypeScript and Photon 2.0, routing group chats (Telegram) and private DMs (iMessage) to a centralized FastAPI backend with sub-second response times.
- **Privacy & Tool-Calling**: Engineered an event-driven multi-agent backend utilizing Grok (xAI) tool-calling loops and SQLite, enforcing strict least-privilege boundaries between public household split rules and private financial balances.
- **Banking Automation**: Integrated the Capital One Nessie API to execute automated rent splits, bill payments, and conditional paybacks, with an auditor module blocking unauthorized figures and private financial leaks.
